It's your bed. Smells like coffee and fish.
Your dad built it thinking you'd grow to be much larger.
It's adorned with the softest of pillows for your weary head.
You like to bury yourself in them and pretend you're in a fortress. 
One of your favorite plushes is permanently deformed with hug-shaped dents. 
The pumpkin plush stares with jealous intent.
Envious gourds.


